+# Holo Gestures Creator-mode Command Bridge Implementation Summary
+
+## Completed Features
+
+### 1. SIGHT: `/api/see` - Screen Capture + OCR
+- **Status**: ✅ Working
+- **Endpoint**: POST `/api/see`
+- **Functionality**: Captures screen and runs OCR to provide text description of what's on screen
+- **Voice Commands**: 
+  - "look at my screen"
+  - "what do you see"
+  - "can you see me"
+- **Brain Endpoint Integration**: Routes through `/api/brain` when these phrases are detected
+
+### 2. VISION: `/api/vision` - Camera Snapshot Endpoint
+- **Status**: ✅ Working  
+- **Endpoint**: GET `/api/vision`
+- **Functionality**: Returns whether a camera frame is available from the user's webcam via the Holo Gestures deck
+- **Added Configuration**: `KF_VISION_ENABLED` environment variable (defaults to "1")
+- **Response**: 
+  - `{"ok": true, "has_image": true, "size": <bytes>}` when camera frame available
+  - `{"ok": false, "error": "no camera frame available"}` when no frame
+
+### 3. BROWSER: `/api/browser` - CDP Automation with Session + Navigation Guard
+- **Status**: ✅ Working
+- **Endpoint**: POST `/api/browser`  
+- **Functionality**: 
+  - Status check: `{"action": "status"}` returns browser attachment status
+  - Navigation: `{"command": "open https://example.com"}` opens URL in attached Chrome
+  - Page reading: `{"command": "read the page"}` extracts visible text via DevTools
+- **Requirements**: Chrome must be started with `--remote-debugging-port=9222 --user-data-dir=/tmp/chrome-debug-profile`
+- **Brain Endpoint Integration**: Routes through `/api/brain` when browser-related phrases detected
+
+### 4. Voice Command Wiring
+- **Status**: ✅ Working
+- **Enhancements to `resolve_intent()` function in `server.py`:**
+  - Added "see" synonyms: ["see", "look", "watch", "vision", "what do you see", "can you see me"] 
+  - Added "browser" synonyms: ["browser", "chrome", "web", "navigate", "open browser", "go to"]
+  - Modified `browser_command()` to detect browser intent from action verbs alone (open/go/navigate/load/visit)
+- **Result**: Phrases like "look at my screen", "what do you see", and "open browser to [url]" now properly route to their respective handlers
+
+### 5. API Documentation Updates
+- **Status**: ✅ Completed
+- **Updated docstring in `server.py`** (lines 8-16) to include new endpoints:
+  ```
+  Endpoints:
+    GET  /               → holo.html
+    GET  /api/notes      → [{name, title, body}] from the folder in holo.json
+                         (falls back to ./sample-notes so it runs instantly)
+    GET  /api/commands   → recent KairoForge Call commands and pending items
+    POST /api/state      → future Jarvis hook: writes state/holo-state.json so the
+                         big brain can react to what the hands did ("Card pinned,
+                         sir"). Nothing reads it yet by design — prototype stays
+                         standalone until proven.
+    POST /api/command-done → marks a queued KairoForge Call command handled
+    GET  /api/vision     → VISION: camera snapshot endpoint so kf can see the user
+                         Returns whether a camera frame is available from the user's
+                         webcam via the Holo Gestures deck
+    GET  /api/see        → SIGHT: screen capture + OCR so kf can describe what's on screen
+    POST /api/browser    → BROWSER: CDP automation with session + navigation guard
