+## 🧠 KairoForge Call
+
+The floating **KairoForge Call** panel near the bottom-right gives Holo a local voice/text
+control surface:
+
+- **Speaker** lets the built-in browser voice talk back.
+- **Talk** listens with browser speech recognition when your browser supports it.
+- **Keyboard** opens a holographic text keyboard. Drag its top bar to move it, use Rotate or
+  +/- to turn and scale it, or pinch with both hands and move in/out to resize it in the air.
+- **Hang up** ends the active call without closing the Holo page.
+
+Try commands like:
+
+```text
+open the keyboard          close the keyboard
+make it bigger             make it smaller
+rotate it                  centre the keyboard
+reset everything           put everything back the way it was
+tidy the board             restore cards
+summarise this             open it
+mute yourself              speaker on
+refresh props              remove selected
+hang up                    jarvis mode
+```
+
+**Anything you say is understood.** kf does not match a fixed list of exact phrases — it
+resolves loose phrasing, synonyms and word order, so "could you pull up the typing pad" is the
+same as "open keyboard".
+
+**And it answers anything else like a person.** Ask it how it's doing, what's on screen, to tell
+you a joke, or who it is — it replies out loud instead of printing a canned help line. That
+conversation runs on a local [Ollama](https://ollama.com) model if one is running, so no API key
+and nothing leaves your machine:
+
+```bash
+ollama pull qwen2.5:7b     # default model
+python3 server.py          # picks it up automatically
+```
+
+Override with environment variables if you use a different model or host:
+
+```bash
+KF_MODEL=gemma4:26b KF_OLLAMA=http://127.0.0.1:11434 python3 server.py
+```
+
+Three layers, in order: **actions** resolve instantly from local rules (no model needed, works
+offline); **live data** answers anything about the real world; everything else goes to the
+**model** for a spoken reply; if no model is reachable it falls back to a plain-language help line
+in milliseconds rather than hanging or going silent.
+
+## 🌍 Real-time answers
+
+kf looks up live facts instead of guessing them — no API key, no account:
+
+```text
+what's the weather like?          what's the weather in Tokyo?
+what time is it in London?        who is Ada Lovelace?
+tell me about the Eiffel Tower    what is quantum computing?
+```
+
+Weather and place lookups use [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com), topic questions use Wikipedia,
+and the clock uses your own system timezone database. Answers are cached for five minutes
+(`KF_CACHE_TTL`) so repeat questions are instant, and every lookup is timeout-guarded — if the
+network is down kf says it could not reach that rather than inventing an answer.
+
+> **macOS note:** python.org Python ships without CA certificates, so outbound HTTPS fails with
+> `CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED` while `curl` still works. kf handles this itself by preferring
+> `certifi` and falling back to `/etc/ssl/cert.pem`. It never disables certificate verification.
+
+## 🖥 Holo Hands inside KairoForge
+
+Say **"open holo hands"** to KairoForge. It starts this server if needed and opens the deck
+full screen inside KairoForge, with the KairoForge orb docked bottom-right. From there you
+can ask KairoForge to put anything on the deck: notes, big text, 3D shapes and models,
+images, live web pages, sandboxed HTML/JS widgets, action buttons, and face/hand sensors.
+It can also wire items together with connectors, so values flow from one item to the next.
+
+Face, hand, and body tracking run on-device. Camera frames never leave the page; only
+derived numbers reach KairoForge. Holo itself runs no shell commands. Anything that
+changes the computer goes through KairoForge and its approval prompts. See
+[SAFETY-COMPUTER-CONTROL.md](SAFETY-COMPUTER-CONTROL.md).
+
+---
