+# kf computer control: removed
+
+Holo no longer runs shell commands. The `KF_ARMED` switch, the `run <command>` phrase,
+and the `/api/exec` endpoint were removed on purpose.
+
+## Where computer control lives now
+
+Holo runs inside KairoForge (say "open holo hands"). KairoForge is the only thing that
+can touch this computer, and it does so through its normal permission and approval
+prompts. On the deck:
+
+- An **action** item sends its prompt to KairoForge as an ordinary request. If that
+  request needs to change files or run something, KairoForge asks first, exactly as it
+  would in chat.
+- **Widgets** are sandboxed (`allow-scripts` only, no network, no same-origin access).
+  They can only exchange values with other items along connectors.
+- **Face, hand, and body tracking** run on-device. Only derived numbers (gesture names,
+  head direction, expression scores) are sent to KairoForge, they are kept in memory
+  only, and they are never written to long-term memory. Camera frames never leave the
+  page.
+
+## What standalone Holo can still do
+
+When you open `http://127.0.0.1:4890` directly (not inside KairoForge), the old call
+panel still has these read-only helpers:
+
+| Endpoint | What it does | Turn off |
+|---|---|---|
+| `POST /api/see` | Screenshot + OCR so kf can describe the screen | `KF_SEE=0` |
+| `POST /api/browser` | Opens a tab or reads page text in a Chrome you started with `--remote-debugging-port` | do not start Chrome with a debugging port |
+| `POST /api/brain` | Local Ollama chat replies | stop Ollama |
+
+None of these run commands. The embedded KairoForge deck does not call them. Requests are
+appended to `state/kf-audit.jsonl`.
